# NOTE: db/migrations, data/golden, docs and all source are TRACKED on purpose.
# They are part of the verified state, not build artifacts.

# Owner-supplied USDA source archives and the large derived branded catalog.
# The catalog is 428 MB of public product data, deterministically regenerable
# from the archive by tools/ingest-branded.py — the checksum manifest and the
# machine report are committed instead.
data/branded-catalog.json

# Full-release branded build outputs (regenerable from the archive by
# tools/ingest-branded.py; ~1 GB). The manifest, report and compact fixtures
# are committed instead.
data/branded/
data/runtime/
data/branded-catalog.json

# Offline catalog bundle (768 MB, regenerable by tools/build-offline-bundle.py).
# The manifest and a bounded real fixture are committed instead.
data/offline-bundle/

# Owner-supplied USDA archives (multi-GB); the README stays tracked.
data/sources/*
!data/sources/README.md

# node_modules is machine-generated; package-lock.json IS tracked when it can be
# generated against a reachable registry (see docs/architecture/PORTABILITY.md).
node_modules/
artifacts/
